+### 6.3 Compatibility tests
+
+`test/integration/release_compatibility_test.rb` (18 tests). It covers:
+
+- R0 and R1 artifacts (session, unwatch link, open-form CSRF token, cache entry) are still read.
+  This includes R1's standard base64 CSRF token.
+- R2 artifacts are still read, and the simulated R3 artifacts are read: the JSON mail envelope, the
+  7.1 cache entries, the session cookie and the CSRF token.
+- What R2 writes can be read by the rollback target: the session cookie (AES-256-GCM with purpose,
+  decrypted the way R1 does it), the unwatch link (legacy envelope, `_rails.message` present, no
+  `_rails.data`) and cache entries (Marshal, `\x04\x08`).
+- The pins are in effect (`load_defaults` version, cookie serializer, key digest, cache format, per-form
+  tokens, origin check, `belongs_to`).
+- A form POST with a different `Origin` is not rejected.
